<title>MEXICO: Mexican tourism to see $1.558 bln investment 97-98.</title>
<headline>Mexican tourism to see $1.558 bln investment 97-98.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's tourism sector will see $1.558 billion in private investment in 1997 and 1998, Tourism Minister Silvia Hernandez said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Plans for 28 investment groups are to invest $1.558 billion in 1997 and 1998,&quot; Hernandez said in a public presentation of the sector's outlook before President Ernesto Zedillo.  </p>
<p>Hernandez said that between 1995 and 1996, 26 groups invested $938 million in Mexico, constructing a total of 12,000 hotel rooms in the period.</p>
<p>She added that the outlook in general for the sector was &quot;very good.  It suffices to say that tourism will grow by at least six percent (in 1997) in terms of visitors and foreign exchange earnings,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>&quot;We will end the year close to $7.3 billion in receipts and we will receive at least 22.5 million tourists, almost one for every Mexican,&quot; she added.</p>
<p>((--Debora Montesinos, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289593))</p>
